WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.750
Racing to save the wounded on the
streets of Strasbourg the city's

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:12.210
world-famous Christmas market now the
site of a deadly mass shooting a gunman

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.010
opened fire on revelers here Tuesday
night before fleeing the scene witnesses

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:24.539
spoke of panic and terrified people as
the shots rang out I saw a lot of people

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:31.529
running scared crying kids and all then
I said I think this must be very very

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:37.440
serious and then when I saw people
crying and the crowd leaving they said

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:44.270
it was a shooting right next door so I
ran away I went to hide in a restaurant

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.809
French president Emanuela McColl held an
emergency meeting with cabinet officials

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:57.660
at the presidential palace afterwards
he tweeted out his condolences saying

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.760
the whole nation stands in solidarity
with Strasbourg our victims and their

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:09.630
families French authorities raised the
terror alert to the highest possible

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:16.220
level as they searched for the 29 year
old shooting suspect unknown criminal

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:24.000
the man is known for civil law offenses
for which he was already condemned in

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.579
France and in Germany the government has
decided to switch to his state of

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:36.990
emergency and reinforced controls at
border crossings we are also stepping up

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:42.240
security at all of the christmas markets
around france to avoid similar events

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:51.030
from happening france has borne the
brunt of some of Europe's worst terror

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:59.460
attacks in recent years now the country
again finds itself in the crosshairs and

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.840
EWS max Hoffman is on the scene he joins
us now max we understand that there has

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.550
been a police operation underway this
morning in downtown Strasbourg what more

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:14.250
have you been seeing there
I am in downtown Strasburg behind me use

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:18.540
we're very close to where all of this
happened last night so where the

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.860
shooting took place you see still see
the Christmas decoration which is part

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.810
of the official Christmas market we are
not aware of a police operation that

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.010
took place if it took place it's not a
very big one as far as we know only one

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.180
media outlet reported it so far with one
source so we're waiting official

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.620
confirmation for that meantime the
French government saying that several

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.010
people allegedly linked to the gunmen
are now in custody do we know anything

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:49.800
more about that yeah Secretary of State
who was interviewed by French media this

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.680
morning said that five people were taken
into custody

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:58.440
connected to that gunman he didn't give
any details who these people were what

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.990
their relation is to the alleged gunman
but the most interesting part of bit of

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:08.700
information to come out of that
interview is that the Secretary of State

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.780
said it wasn't impossible that the
gunman might have left as he called it

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:18.180
the territory which means that he might
be on his way or already in Germany you

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.200
have to keep in mind Strasbourg is right
on the border with Germany and this gun

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.700
man has a history in Germany he was not
only condemned for crimes here in France

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:32.370
but also in neighboring Germany who is
he max because I mean we are starting to

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:39.090
get some more details some more
specifics about him he's 29 years old

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.230
he's very well known to the authorities
because as I said earlier he was already

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:48.510
condemned in France in Germany served
some prison time but not for deeds

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:55.410
related to terrorism criminal acts theft
and in fact that man was supposed to be

00:03:55.410 --> 00:04:00.510
taken into custody on Tuesday morning
because of attempted homicide that's the

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.340
reason why the police went to take him
into custody he was not at home they

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:11.489
found an assault rifle at his house as
we understand but since they couldn't

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:16.140
take him into custody he was free to you
know to do what he did on Tuesday

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:21.690
evening so the same day here in
Strasbourg he apparently I mean when we

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.420
talk about the actual incident he
managed to get inside a security zone

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.810
around the Christmas market and max I
know that you you have visited those

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:32.920
Christmas markets you're quite familiar
with the security there how do you think

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:39.640
he might have been able to get through
well the French may the the mayor of

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:43.920
Strasbourg himself was at a loss he said
I don't know how he managed to do that

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.880
the controls here were pretty thorough
when we got here on Monday the streets

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:53.140
leading up to the Christmas market were
controlled the cars were some cars were

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.310
stopped people were had to get out they
had to show what they had in the trunks

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:02.230
so the authorities were on it and we
know that a couple hundred police

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:06.580
officers were always controlling the
area also soldiers because the military

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:11.860
is allowed to operate in cities in
France but of course you know with a

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:17.200
with the number of visitors in a city
like Strasbourg I would think that it's

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:22.420
impossible to have complete control over
the situation but I'm sure that the

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.600
authorities will try to figure out what
exactly happened and how the gunman was

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:31.450
able to smuggle in his rifle and we know
he is still at large at this hour GWS

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:35.880
max Wolfman with the latest from
Strasbourg Thank You max

